# The sound sets, one per line. scripts/pin.sh turns this into sets.txt (every
# file, with its address and SHA-256). Fields, separated by |:
#
#   id | name | role | licence | credit | GitHub repository | ref | the
#   instrument's .sfz in it | what to call it once installed | notice
#
# ref is a commit (the sets stay as they were pinned until it is changed).
# One instrument per set, no variations: only the one .sfz named here is
# kept (renamed, nothing inside it is changed), with the files it plays and
# the licence and readme. Every set is credited, whatever its licence. The
# notice is text a licence asks to be shown (empty when none).
#
# role is one of electric-guitars, acoustic-guitars, basses, drums.
